"""Balatro 1.0.1o item pools in EXACT in-game order.  Pure data, no logic.

Source of truth: the game's own ``Game:init_item_prototypes`` (game.lua:216-843) executed
in LuaJIT 2.1 (lupa) with stubbed globals, then ``P_CENTER_POOLS`` / ``P_JOKER_RARITY_POOLS``
dumped after the game's own ``table.sort`` calls (game.lua:826-842).  The lists below are
those arrays verbatim; nothing here was ordered by hand.  See NOTES_POOLS.md for the sort
rule, the hash-ordered exceptions, and the mapping to ``balatro_sim``.

Conventions
-----------
* Every list is in pool index order: ``LIST[i-1]`` is Lua ``pool[i]``, which is what
  ``pseudorandom_element(pool, ...)`` indexes with ``math.random(#pool)``.
* ``unlocked`` is the PROFILE DEFAULT (fresh save).  Consumables carry ``None`` because the
  Lua prototype has no ``unlocked`` field at all; the game's eligibility test is
  ``v.unlocked ~= false or v.rarity == 4`` so ``None`` counts as unlocked.  MLB ranked play
  assumes a fully unlocked profile: treat every ``False`` as ``True`` for that ruleset.
* ``discovered`` is likewise the fresh-profile default.  It matters only for Tag eligibility
  (``tag.requires`` must be *discovered*) and the collection UI.
* ``config`` is the prototype's ``config`` table verbatim (numbers as Lua doubles; integral
  values are emitted as Python ints).
* Keys are the game's own string keys (``j_``, ``c_``, ``v_``, ``p_``, ``b_``, ``m_``, ``e_``,
  ``bl_``, ``tag_``, ``stake_``).  They are what ``pseudorandom_element`` returns from a pool.

Generated by scratchpad/gen_pools.py from prototypes.json.  Regenerate rather than hand-edit.
"""

